laurel 2782: IPA v4.2 (GSI 2.2): the AP allocates all GSI channels, the modem's too, before QMI INIT_MODEM_DRIVER (ipa3_post_init -> ipa3_alloc_gsi_channel; mainline gsi.c modem_alloc): 2780 did not, and the modem firmware asserted ipa_hal.c:6001 "Failed to initialize GSI channel: CHID 1 errval 6" 105 ms after INIT_MODEM_DRIVER, which stopped Wi-Fi (USB log 2026-11-01 17:01). New: bsd/dev/laurel_ipa_gsi.c (gsi_register_device without an interrupt handler + channel table of ipa3_ep_mapping[IPA_4_2] in pipe order; polled: EE 0 channels GSI_CH_ALLOCATE + context state, EE 1/2 generic command ALLOCATE with return code 1 as the only proof). laurel_ipa_link.c = the QMI 0x31 part of laurel_ipa.c, unchanged but for its last look at GSI_STATUS before NEW_SERVER. Self-checks before the modem hears of the IPA: registers, version and SHARED_MEM_SIZE read again after the firmware (stock reads them after it), IPA_ENABLED_PIPES and channels per EE, every channel allocated, GSI ERROR_LOG 0, every local memory word read back, SMEM 497. A failure: LAUREL IPA: off: <why>, no message to the modem. A modem assert after INIT_MODEM_DRIVER remains possible: docs/laurel_sprout/cellular.md section 8; uefi-image.sh keeps ipa=0 until a phone boot shows the evidence listed there.

